WEBVTT

00:00:27.960 --> 00:00:32.760
Azazel-type, code name Walker,
has made contact with Welle Shield 1.

00:00:32.760 --> 00:00:34.220
The shield will be neutralized.

00:00:41.560 --> 00:00:44.180
Seventeen enemies invading Tatsumiyajima.

00:00:44.180 --> 00:00:46.520
Maintain course. Hold them off
with conventional weaponry.

00:00:46.520 --> 00:00:48.400
A vanguard force?

00:00:48.400 --> 00:00:52.690
They propagate, transform the environment,
and accumulate information.

00:00:52.690 --> 00:00:54.030
That's Mir itself.

00:01:01.620 --> 00:01:02.580
Ready, on standby!

00:01:03.700 --> 00:01:06.040
I'm going, Sis.

00:01:06.040 --> 00:01:09.000
Mark Sechs mod, code name Amaterasu, deploy!

00:01:13.950 --> 00:01:16.380
That's the sixteenth machine. It isn't Toumi...

00:01:16.380 --> 00:01:19.640
Having him lure the enemy on first engage?

00:01:19.640 --> 00:01:20.680
That's a high hurdle.

00:01:24.220 --> 00:01:24.920
Nice!

00:01:24.920 --> 00:01:25.950
He's keeping calm.

00:01:25.950 --> 00:01:26.560
Yeah.

00:01:27.270 --> 00:01:29.520
Luring the enemy with only one mech?

00:01:29.520 --> 00:01:34.200
In every battle, someone takes that role.

00:01:34.200 --> 00:01:36.240
What reckless courage.

00:01:36.240 --> 00:01:39.350
Mommy, I don't feel good...

00:01:39.350 --> 00:01:42.200
Don't worry. The medicine will kick in soon.

00:01:45.160 --> 00:01:48.150
Don't let their hatred swallow you up.

00:01:48.860 --> 00:01:52.630
Build a wall in your heart, like the
one around your island.

00:01:55.670 --> 00:01:58.590
Why do they hate me?

00:01:59.940 --> 00:02:00.550
Miwa...

00:02:00.990 --> 00:02:02.510
You aren't alone.

00:02:03.090 --> 00:02:07.400
The world is trying to get rid of everyone
who can talk with them.

00:03:42.160 --> 00:03:45.370
It's a Sphinx-type, but it isn't
trying to make mental contact.

00:03:46.170 --> 00:03:47.490
Has it already learned?

00:03:47.970 --> 00:03:48.830
What is it doing?

00:03:54.470 --> 00:03:56.010
He succeeded in luring the enemy!

00:03:56.010 --> 00:03:58.420
Deploy shield! Set up battlefield!

00:04:02.920 --> 00:04:04.550
Fafner unit, advance!

00:04:04.550 --> 00:04:06.180
Here I go.

00:04:06.180 --> 00:04:08.510
Gobain!

00:04:19.690 --> 00:04:22.150
Fafner unit, engage Alt Dog!

00:04:27.980 --> 00:04:29.410
The long-range type is in front.

00:04:30.130 --> 00:04:31.620
What's the one in back?

00:04:31.620 --> 00:04:34.540
Fall back. Cover the ground unit.

00:04:34.920 --> 00:04:36.390
Requesting change of strategy.

00:04:36.390 --> 00:04:37.000
What?

00:04:38.460 --> 00:04:40.950
The enemy has captured the base without invasion.

00:04:40.950 --> 00:04:43.420
I propose immediate dissolution
of the defense unit.

00:04:43.740 --> 00:04:46.390
The base... The defense unit?

00:04:46.630 --> 00:04:47.320
Sui-chan!

00:04:47.320 --> 00:04:47.850
Sui!

00:04:49.110 --> 00:04:50.180
Wait a minute!

00:04:51.140 --> 00:04:53.350
Kaburagi, you idiot!

00:04:53.640 --> 00:04:54.900
He's acting on his own!

00:04:54.900 --> 00:04:57.560
It's because of that weird stuff you said, Kazuki!

00:04:58.130 --> 00:04:59.020
No...

00:04:59.250 --> 00:05:01.210
Tsukuyomi, Susanoo, forward.

00:05:01.210 --> 00:05:02.990
Zwölf, Neun, ready scepter.

00:05:06.800 --> 00:05:10.130
With that enemy's shield,
just firing isn't enough...

00:05:10.740 --> 00:05:12.410
I have to match the wavelength with my weapon.

00:05:34.390 --> 00:05:36.350
You're using the Gundrake that way?

00:05:41.310 --> 00:05:43.280
The mobile samurai is here!

00:05:43.280 --> 00:05:44.310
Take this.

00:05:44.310 --> 00:05:46.240
Gobain Crash!

00:06:02.970 --> 00:06:05.550
Gobain program, startup complete.

00:06:05.550 --> 00:06:07.510
There's no such program.

00:06:07.510 --> 00:06:09.140
He's attacking with his shield.

00:06:09.140 --> 00:06:10.720
Way to go, third generation!

00:06:20.510 --> 00:06:21.190
That's one.

00:06:27.070 --> 00:06:27.990
Two.

00:06:29.790 --> 00:06:30.450
Three...

00:06:34.630 --> 00:06:36.780
They're doing everything right.

00:06:36.780 --> 00:06:39.220
Won't their altered consciousness confuse them?

00:06:39.220 --> 00:06:43.630
No. Someone is holding their formation,
so they don't take a concentrated attack.

00:06:43.990 --> 00:06:46.460
The enemy has taken a defensive
stance within the shield.

00:06:46.670 --> 00:06:48.470
It knew it would be trapped inside.

00:06:48.720 --> 00:06:50.340
Then our target is...

00:06:55.540 --> 00:06:57.770
Unknown field erupting at the battle site.

00:06:57.770 --> 00:06:59.270
Shield rapidly failing!

00:07:14.350 --> 00:07:17.290
Welle Shields 3, 4, and 2 have been penetrated.

00:07:17.290 --> 00:07:18.540
Welle Shield 6 is shot.

00:07:18.840 --> 00:07:21.680
A two-stage attack, to bombard us
and destroy the shields?

00:07:22.260 --> 00:07:25.930
They've learned the island's strategy
and weaknesses in one battle.

00:07:26.500 --> 00:07:28.510
They've never been known to learn that quickly.

00:07:28.760 --> 00:07:32.090
Estimating damage if all shields
through 8 are destroyed.

00:07:32.580 --> 00:07:34.250
It would shoot through the
Tatsumiyajima mainland,

00:07:34.250 --> 00:07:36.480
hitting the CDC and keel block directly.

00:07:36.480 --> 00:07:39.060
Countermeasures would require
several hours to prepare.

00:07:39.060 --> 00:07:41.520
The whole island would sink in
fewer than five seconds.

00:07:42.310 --> 00:07:44.080
Stop the enemy within two minutes.

00:07:44.080 --> 00:07:46.930
If that's impossible, move the combat
zone away from the mainland.

00:07:46.930 --> 00:07:47.480
Roger.

00:07:48.380 --> 00:07:51.450
I guess, worst case, we'll have
to abandon the Fafner unit...

00:07:54.690 --> 00:07:57.300
Defeat the enemy within two
minutes. Any thoughts?

00:07:57.300 --> 00:08:00.020
Is the block ready to be cut off
from the island, just in case?

00:08:00.020 --> 00:08:01.210
It's ready.

00:08:01.900 --> 00:08:03.330
That's a relief.

00:08:03.330 --> 00:08:05.850
Even if we're eliminated, the island will survive.

00:08:06.410 --> 00:08:07.130
And...

00:08:07.680 --> 00:08:09.090
There's plenty of time!

00:08:12.660 --> 00:08:13.800
This is checkmate.

00:08:19.240 --> 00:08:21.990
Enemy defense halved.
Requesting backup for interception.

00:08:22.520 --> 00:08:24.090
Senior pilots, attack from the flanks,

00:08:24.090 --> 00:08:25.480
and we'll go in from the front!

00:08:25.750 --> 00:08:26.710
Got it.

00:08:26.710 --> 00:08:28.610
Intercept system, target.

00:08:28.610 --> 00:08:30.440
Zwölf, Neun, right forward!

00:08:32.380 --> 00:08:34.400
I can't believe I'm taking orders...

00:09:02.430 --> 00:09:05.750
Damn you!

00:09:07.320 --> 00:09:08.250
Mimika!

00:09:09.820 --> 00:09:11.980
You've lost!

00:09:14.280 --> 00:09:14.780
Reo-chan!

00:09:51.360 --> 00:09:53.570
Welle Shield 8 penetrated!

00:09:53.570 --> 00:09:54.830
Direct hit on Mukou Island.

00:09:54.830 --> 00:09:56.530
Assessing damage.

00:10:09.250 --> 00:10:10.130
Rina-san!

00:10:14.590 --> 00:10:17.250
Just get the hell out of here!

00:10:27.750 --> 00:10:30.480
Super final attack: Gou Spark.

00:10:30.480 --> 00:10:31.940
There's no such thing.

00:10:33.760 --> 00:10:35.690
You're amazing, Nishio-sensei.

00:10:35.690 --> 00:10:39.390
This really was used as educational material.

00:10:39.390 --> 00:10:40.360
Yeah, well...

00:10:53.970 --> 00:10:55.810
They stopped the Azazel-type...

00:10:55.810 --> 00:10:57.710
So that's the power of D Island,

00:10:57.710 --> 00:11:00.220
which the Neo United Nations leaders
feared and tried to take?

00:11:00.220 --> 00:11:02.370
The way they fight is unbelievable.

00:11:02.370 --> 00:11:04.420
I don't know if I should praise or scold them...

00:11:04.420 --> 00:11:06.340
And their mechs' performance is beyond comparison.

00:11:06.340 --> 00:11:07.560
The pilots are outstanding, too.

00:11:08.310 --> 00:11:10.420
We really will be retiring now.

00:11:11.520 --> 00:11:12.520
Yeah.

00:11:12.520 --> 00:11:15.350
Well done. Everyone, head back.

00:11:15.350 --> 00:11:18.660
Um... I apologize for disregarding the plan.

00:11:18.660 --> 00:11:21.220
No, your proposal and actions were appropriate.

00:11:21.750 --> 00:11:23.490
I'm glad you have faith in me!

00:11:23.490 --> 00:11:25.900
There's no guarantee you'll
be sent out next time.

00:11:25.900 --> 00:11:27.910
Head back for your medical checkup.

00:11:27.910 --> 00:11:28.650
Right!

00:11:32.270 --> 00:11:34.050
The successor to the system, huh?

00:11:34.840 --> 00:11:36.370
Guess I'll be retiring, too.

00:11:40.150 --> 00:11:40.980
Want one?

00:11:43.940 --> 00:11:44.700
Sure.

00:11:47.900 --> 00:11:49.640
I guess I was a little nervous...

00:11:50.780 --> 00:11:51.730
Same here.

00:11:51.730 --> 00:11:53.350
Great fight, everyone.

00:11:53.650 --> 00:11:54.810
Hiroto-senpai!

00:11:54.810 --> 00:11:58.020
I'm trusting you to protect the island's
peace, third generation.

00:11:58.590 --> 00:11:59.860
Mimika, roger!

00:12:02.070 --> 00:12:03.960
Good morning, Tatsumiyajima!

00:12:03.960 --> 00:12:06.090
This is everyone's idol, Douma Hiroto, and...

00:12:06.090 --> 00:12:07.330
Tatekami Seri.

00:12:07.330 --> 00:12:09.540
Hey, why are we dressed like this?

00:12:09.800 --> 00:12:13.060
To help the Human Army understand
our culture, of course.

00:12:13.060 --> 00:12:15.160
Right now, they're a hot topic.

00:12:15.160 --> 00:12:16.150
Eh? For real?

00:12:16.150 --> 00:12:17.540
Let's interview!

00:12:18.190 --> 00:12:20.850
To think journalism still exists in this age...

00:12:20.850 --> 00:12:23.180
This is truly a remarkable island.

00:12:23.180 --> 00:12:24.710
It's nothing that special...

00:12:24.710 --> 00:12:27.550
Why did you come to this island, General?

00:12:27.550 --> 00:12:32.300
The Esperanto guided us here to tell
the island of its hope and crisis.

00:12:32.300 --> 00:12:34.240
What do you mean by "hope"?

00:12:34.240 --> 00:12:36.790
Conversation with Mir, the core
of the enemy's consciousness,

00:12:36.790 --> 00:12:39.910
to transform it into something
beneficial to humanity.

00:12:39.910 --> 00:12:42.230
We wish to bring together the Esperanto,
who possess that power

00:12:42.230 --> 00:12:43.490
and prevent the crisis.

00:12:43.490 --> 00:12:44.800
Crisis?

00:12:44.800 --> 00:12:47.890
A new Mir is approaching this planet.

00:12:47.890 --> 00:12:51.850
Our Mir can contact it faster
than any other being.

00:12:52.340 --> 00:12:54.290
And with the power of the Esperanto,

00:12:54.290 --> 00:12:57.220
we will make this new Mir our ally.

00:12:57.220 --> 00:12:59.320
What do you mean by "our Mir"?

00:12:59.320 --> 00:13:03.010
The fragment of Mir within Emery,
which has fully grown.

00:13:03.730 --> 00:13:06.180
The sacred Ashoka.

00:13:06.180 --> 00:13:07.840
Some also call it the World Tree.

00:13:07.840 --> 00:13:10.440
This is the Esperanto who
led General Narain here,

00:13:10.440 --> 00:13:12.060
Emery Almond-san.

00:13:12.560 --> 00:13:14.890
So you raised a Mir?

00:13:15.570 --> 00:13:17.430
Along with lots of other friends.

00:13:18.170 --> 00:13:22.070
But it was my little brother who first
taught me how to talk with it.

00:13:22.070 --> 00:13:23.190
Where is your little brother?

00:13:24.130 --> 00:13:27.540
Everyone in my family became part of the Mir.

00:13:27.960 --> 00:13:30.050
To erase all the hatred from the enemy.

00:13:31.110 --> 00:13:34.040
Then, is that shoe...

00:13:34.040 --> 00:13:35.690
It's my brother's.

00:13:36.100 --> 00:13:39.830
His health was poor, so he couldn't go outside.

00:13:39.830 --> 00:13:41.190
He used to say that when he grew up,

00:13:41.190 --> 00:13:43.890
he wanted to wear these,
and walk all around the world.

00:13:44.390 --> 00:13:46.020
And the other shoe?

00:13:46.020 --> 00:13:47.510
I buried it in our hometown,

00:13:48.240 --> 00:13:51.930
so he can walk all around the world
with me, while he stays at home.

00:13:52.230 --> 00:13:55.890
I'm going to tell it that it's good
when everyone's together.

00:13:56.930 --> 00:13:59.860
That if everyone hates everyone else,
no one will be left.

00:14:00.130 --> 00:14:02.670
The expeditionary force is
expected to become a reality.

00:14:02.670 --> 00:14:05.330
Naturally, we foresee no sacrifices.

00:14:05.330 --> 00:14:08.100
This island had become hidden, even from humanity.

00:14:08.100 --> 00:14:10.770
Why have you decided to
interact with them now?

00:14:11.190 --> 00:14:13.050
Because we share the same goal.

00:14:13.480 --> 00:14:17.750
If the enemy Mir and humanity can
coexist, the fighting will end.

00:14:17.750 --> 00:14:18.180
Nishio Shop

00:14:18.180 --> 00:14:21.410
This is Nishio Akira-san, an applicant
for the expeditionary force.

00:14:21.410 --> 00:14:23.950
Since it was decided that I'm really
going, I've been so nervous.

00:14:23.950 --> 00:14:26.230
It's tough having an idiot for a brother.

00:14:26.230 --> 00:14:27.360
I could say the same about you!

00:14:27.360 --> 00:14:28.640
What?!

00:14:28.640 --> 00:14:29.680
No fighting!

00:14:29.890 --> 00:14:31.840
I don't trust the Human Army!

00:14:32.340 --> 00:14:35.660
But it was Commander Makabe's decision,
so there's nothing I can do.

00:14:35.660 --> 00:14:39.140
I'll keep an eye on things here,
so you'd better come back safe!

00:14:39.470 --> 00:14:42.390
This is the expedition leader,
Mizoguchi Kyousuke-san.

00:14:42.390 --> 00:14:44.170
We take the fewest members possible,

00:14:44.170 --> 00:14:47.850
accomplish our goal quickly,
and hurry home. That's it.

00:14:47.850 --> 00:14:49.240
Is everything ready?

00:14:49.690 --> 00:14:50.550
Yep.

00:14:50.550 --> 00:14:53.470
We've selected the members, calculated the
fuel we'll need, and chosen the gear.

00:14:53.470 --> 00:14:55.700
That's the fruit of many years of experience.

00:14:55.700 --> 00:14:58.650
Mizoguchi-san made me do all of that!

00:14:59.060 --> 00:15:00.920
He trusts you, Saki.

00:15:00.920 --> 00:15:03.570
You've always excelled at what you do.

00:15:03.570 --> 00:15:05.350
Here, Mai-Mai's snack set.

00:15:05.350 --> 00:15:07.940
And yet, he didn't pick me to go!

00:15:08.530 --> 00:15:10.010
He's terrible.

00:15:10.010 --> 00:15:11.840
I wanna go, too!

00:15:11.840 --> 00:15:14.350
Now, Saki-chan, never you mind.

00:15:14.350 --> 00:15:16.380
There it is! Her "never you Mai-nd"!

00:15:16.380 --> 00:15:19.360
I love it. Gotta hear it at least once a day!

00:15:19.360 --> 00:15:21.350
So you're also staying behind, Mitsugu-kun?

00:15:21.350 --> 00:15:23.810
Yeah, I'm on duty at Takeru Island, as always.

00:15:23.810 --> 00:15:26.540
You're the next captain, aren't you? Impressive!

00:15:26.540 --> 00:15:29.010
If you can marry her soon,
it'll put me at ease, too—

00:15:29.010 --> 00:15:30.280
Dad!

00:15:31.500 --> 00:15:34.240
Lucky... Wish I had a nice guy, too.

00:15:37.060 --> 00:15:37.740
I'm back!

00:15:37.740 --> 00:15:39.160
Hiro-chan, welcome back.

00:15:39.160 --> 00:15:42.620
...of the transport craft. I trust the force
to do its job and come home safe.

00:15:42.620 --> 00:15:44.110
Ta-dah!

00:15:44.110 --> 00:15:45.590
It's official!

00:15:45.850 --> 00:15:47.890
You're going with the expeditionary force?

00:15:47.890 --> 00:15:50.250
Why? Do you hate the island, Hiro-chan?

00:15:50.250 --> 00:15:53.870
No, Sis... I'll bring the island
and the world together.

00:15:53.870 --> 00:15:57.160
Through mutual understanding,
fighting among humans will cease.

00:15:57.160 --> 00:16:00.270
And that's a job for this island's idol, me!

00:16:00.480 --> 00:16:02.690
Hiroto, you've grown so much...

00:16:02.690 --> 00:16:04.230
What about Seri-chan?

00:16:04.550 --> 00:16:07.070
She'll be fine... Wait, she has
nothing to do with this!

00:16:07.070 --> 00:16:07.280
Didn't you say you were curious about her?

00:16:07.280 --> 00:16:08.470
This is Toumi Maya-san.

00:16:08.470 --> 00:16:08.960
Didn't you say you were curious about her?

00:16:08.960 --> 00:16:09.190
That was when we were kids!

00:16:09.190 --> 00:16:10.780
Yes, I applied.

00:16:10.780 --> 00:16:11.180
The People's Restaurant

00:16:11.180 --> 00:16:13.770
Fighting is all I can do.

00:16:13.770 --> 00:16:17.510
If there's another way, I'd like to
hear it, and I want to help.
The People's Restaurant

00:16:17.510 --> 00:16:18.240
The People's Restaurant

00:16:18.240 --> 00:16:18.740
Hey...

00:16:18.740 --> 00:16:19.950
Nope.

00:16:20.890 --> 00:16:22.910
I didn't even say anything.

00:16:23.350 --> 00:16:25.330
You're staying behind.

00:16:25.330 --> 00:16:28.360
Didn't old man Makabe and
Mizoguchi-san tell you, too?

00:16:28.360 --> 00:16:30.900
I know. I'd just hold them back.

00:16:30.900 --> 00:16:34.150
That isn't why... You need to stay on the island,

00:16:34.150 --> 00:16:35.840
the place we'll be coming home to.

00:16:36.210 --> 00:16:38.320
Do you really think it's possible?

00:16:39.250 --> 00:16:43.810
Making the approaching enemy an
ally before the battle can begin?

00:16:44.280 --> 00:16:45.450
I don't know.

00:16:45.970 --> 00:16:49.360
But if there's hope that we can have peace,

00:16:49.360 --> 00:16:51.500
then there's a reason to fight.

00:16:53.300 --> 00:16:53.890
Yeah.

00:16:56.620 --> 00:16:58.200
It's all a contradiction, huh?

00:16:58.730 --> 00:17:02.080
We hurt others because we want peace,

00:17:02.680 --> 00:17:04.710
and the cycle repeats over and over.

00:17:05.530 --> 00:17:08.540
If you find a way to end it,
I want to know what it is.

00:17:10.440 --> 00:17:12.140
I want to know what I can do.

00:17:12.140 --> 00:17:12.800
Yeah.

00:17:14.520 --> 00:17:16.510
You'll be the first one I tell.

00:17:20.120 --> 00:17:20.970
Be careful.

00:17:23.130 --> 00:17:23.770
Yeah.

00:17:29.620 --> 00:17:30.610
Hey...

00:17:30.610 --> 00:17:32.650
Can I take this with me?

00:17:32.650 --> 00:17:35.030
Sure. Your mommy said you could.

00:17:35.030 --> 00:17:37.570
Yay! Isn't that great, Mako-chan?

00:17:38.570 --> 00:17:41.530
Miwa told me to take it for protection,

00:17:41.530 --> 00:17:43.970
so I had Mikado-san resize it for me.

00:17:44.720 --> 00:17:46.930
Miwa is our daughter.

00:17:46.930 --> 00:17:48.390
I swear I'll protect her.

00:17:51.050 --> 00:17:52.670
I'll now announce the expeditionary force members.

00:17:53.140 --> 00:17:58.060
For the Fafner unit: Toumi Maya,
Nishio Akira, Douma Hiroto.

00:17:58.060 --> 00:17:59.570
For the CDC: Olga Betrenko.

00:17:59.570 --> 00:18:00.790
A younger brother, huh?

00:18:00.790 --> 00:18:01.890
For Takeru Island...

00:18:02.230 --> 00:18:04.490
To victory and hope!

00:18:04.490 --> 00:18:05.930
Cheers!

00:18:13.340 --> 00:18:15.780
Don't worry. We'll protect the island.

00:18:20.550 --> 00:18:21.340
Seri...

00:18:22.810 --> 00:18:25.350
What are you doing? You missed the toast.

00:18:26.720 --> 00:18:27.410
I just

00:18:28.490 --> 00:18:30.790
don't really care for noisy crowds.

00:18:31.880 --> 00:18:35.320
Did Minashiro Tsubaki tell you to be alone?

00:18:36.520 --> 00:18:37.340
No.

00:18:38.470 --> 00:18:41.250
We all watched her sacrifice together.

00:18:42.420 --> 00:18:44.310
Don't carry this by yourself.

00:18:44.570 --> 00:18:47.270
I'm not, really.

00:18:47.870 --> 00:18:50.630
Let's go join the others.

00:18:50.630 --> 00:18:52.920
Sure, in a bit.

00:18:53.540 --> 00:18:54.230
Here.

00:18:55.960 --> 00:18:58.210
Be sure you toast with everyone else later.

00:18:58.210 --> 00:18:59.200
Okay.

00:19:04.050 --> 00:19:05.120
Take care.

00:19:06.020 --> 00:19:10.710
I'll return with hope that will make
you and Minashiro Tsubaki happy.

00:19:12.010 --> 00:19:12.810
I'll be waiting.

00:19:14.960 --> 00:19:16.650
Did you talk to Kazuki?

00:19:17.090 --> 00:19:19.760
He wanted to go, so I told him he couldn't.

00:19:20.200 --> 00:19:22.090
If you told him that, he'll give up.

00:19:22.880 --> 00:19:25.050
If you think you can't trust them,
pull back right away.

00:19:25.890 --> 00:19:27.020
You don't trust them?

00:19:27.260 --> 00:19:28.720
I'm willing to gamble on the possibility,

00:19:29.230 --> 00:19:31.480
but the status of humanity
as a whole is uncertain.

00:19:32.670 --> 00:19:34.150
You be the judge.

00:19:35.250 --> 00:19:36.440
For all our sakes.

00:19:38.020 --> 00:19:38.900
Yeah.

00:19:40.360 --> 00:19:42.280
Did you talk to Maya?

00:19:42.700 --> 00:19:44.820
She told me to stay behind.

00:19:45.070 --> 00:19:49.880
Of course she did. I'll keep an eye on you
to make sure you don't leave the island.

00:19:49.880 --> 00:19:51.990
Oh, yeah... I could just leave.

00:19:51.990 --> 00:19:53.170
I'm telling you not to!

00:19:54.130 --> 00:19:55.130
I was kidding.

00:19:56.290 --> 00:19:58.950
Maya's being taken off regular pilot duty.

00:19:58.950 --> 00:20:01.210
This will probably be her last mission.

00:20:01.910 --> 00:20:05.590
You and Maya should both
spend more time in peace.

00:20:11.420 --> 00:20:15.480
How will I bless the world...

00:20:18.230 --> 00:20:20.320
Come on in.

00:20:21.770 --> 00:20:24.070
I heard the pilots were here...

00:20:30.730 --> 00:20:32.090
Did I interrupt something?

00:20:40.530 --> 00:20:42.720
Take care of Toumi and the others.

00:20:46.920 --> 00:20:50.180
I swear on this body, which was given your factor.

00:21:14.170 --> 00:21:15.620
No response from Solomon.

00:21:15.620 --> 00:21:18.080
The defensive force has arrived
at the planned point.

00:21:18.080 --> 00:21:21.670
Partial removal of Welle Shield 1 at 01-28.

00:21:22.020 --> 00:21:23.590
Permission to depart granted.

00:21:58.560 --> 00:22:01.960
You have one month. I pray you'll
have a safe journey.

00:23:36.380 --> 00:23:38.470
We've got about ninety percent back.

00:23:38.470 --> 00:23:41.610
Looks like we'll make it in
time for the festival today.

00:23:41.610 --> 00:23:43.440
Kazuki-senpai, are you done?

00:23:44.910 --> 00:23:45.860
Almost.

00:23:45.860 --> 00:23:47.860
You're thinking too much.

00:23:47.860 --> 00:23:50.320
Just write the wish you want granted most.

00:23:51.420 --> 00:23:52.170
Right.

00:24:02.560 --> 00:24:04.470
We gambled on the possibility.

00:24:05.390 --> 00:24:07.370
It was indeed hope,

00:24:07.970 --> 00:24:09.670
but it was not the path to peace.

00:24:11.270 --> 00:24:13.460
When the first sacrifice departed,

00:24:14.080 --> 00:24:17.860
the island once again welcomed hope and crisis.

00:24:22.500 --> 00:24:25.410
<i>Fafner in the Azure: Exodus</i>, episode 6:

00:24:25.410 --> 00:24:26.980
Blessed Time.
